1
0:00:00,400 --> 0:00:03,590
I asked an AI shopping assistant for a purple table runner.

2
0:00:03,470 --> 0:00:04,940
Twice, at the same moment.

3
0:00:07,900 --> 0:00:10,570
On the left, it sees only the listings.

4
0:00:10,450 --> 0:00:14,030
It picks Violet and Vine: linen, cheaper, ships fast.

5
0:00:14,500 --> 0:00:17,810
On the right, it can check each shop's record. It picks Lydia.

6
0:00:18,200 --> 0:00:20,320
What the left side could not see:

7
0:00:20,200 --> 0:00:22,560
Violet and Vine's seal was withdrawn.

8
0:00:22,440 --> 0:00:24,990
Buyers got polyester, or nothing at all.

9
0:00:25,600 --> 0:00:27,320
We ran fifty requests like that.

10
0:00:27,800 --> 0:00:31,380
Without evidence, shops like that won thirty-four times.

11
0:00:31,260 --> 0:00:32,610
With evidence, zero.

12
0:00:33,100 --> 0:00:35,880
Honest small shops went from nine wins to thirty-five.

13
0:00:36,600 --> 0:00:41,980
A study this fall found AI assistants choose the big chain about nine times in ten.

14
0:00:43,000 --> 0:00:44,580
This is Real Deal Seal.

15
0:00:44,460 --> 0:00:48,070
It turns a small shop's PayPal history into a passport.

16
0:00:48,700 --> 0:00:51,260
It is not a score. It counts what happened:

17
0:00:51,140 --> 0:00:53,810
orders completed, shipments tracked, refunds.

18
0:00:54,400 --> 0:00:56,510
Every fact says where it came from:

19
0:00:56,390 --> 0:01:00,040
PayPal's records, the shop itself, or simulated for this demo.

20
0:01:05,000 --> 0:01:08,420
The passport is signed, so anyone can check it. Genuine.

21
0:01:10,600 --> 0:01:12,690
Change one number, and the check fails.

22
0:01:15,200 --> 0:01:17,430
This badge was never signed by us: forged.

23
0:01:18,300 --> 0:01:21,550
And when we withdraw a seal, the old badge stops working.

24
0:01:21,900 --> 0:01:25,560
Plain code decides this. No AI model is involved.

25
0:01:26,200 --> 0:01:27,830
The agent finishes the job.

26
0:01:27,710 --> 0:01:30,390
It opens a PayPal checkout for Lydia's runner.

27
0:01:30,900 --> 0:01:33,770
But only I can approve the payment, on PayPal's own page.

28
0:01:34,300 --> 0:01:38,290
Then our server asks PayPal whether that exact amount was captured.

29
0:01:38,170 --> 0:01:39,500
Only then is it paid.

30
0:01:40,300 --> 0:01:43,180
This is the PayPal sandbox, with test money.

31
0:01:43,060 --> 0:01:47,070
For a shop whose seal was withdrawn, checkout is switched off.

32
0:01:52,000 --> 0:01:53,470
Shop owners get a studio.

33
0:01:55,800 --> 0:01:57,490
Martha misses four rules.

34
0:01:57,370 --> 0:02:01,700
One click shows the exact orders behind each number, in an AG Grid.

35
0:02:05,400 --> 0:02:08,610
She adds a tracking number, and her count goes up by one.

36
0:02:08,490 --> 0:02:10,610
The record shows it before and after.

37
0:02:12,800 --> 0:02:14,080
We tested it hard.

38
0:02:13,960 --> 0:02:20,190
Fifty requests and eleven attacks, written before any run, on two models, three full runs each.

39
0:02:22,200 --> 0:02:25,610
Forged seals, edited seals, hidden instructions, pressure.

40
0:02:26,100 --> 0:02:30,260
Every single run is published in an AG Grid you can filter and export:

41
0:02:30,140 --> 0:02:34,480
six hundred picks, including the ones we re-ran after fixing our own bug.

42
0:02:35,100 --> 0:02:35,750
Under it:

43
0:02:35,630 --> 0:02:41,330
eight agent tools over MCP, and a data platform where every promise is checked on every build.

44
0:02:45,000 --> 0:02:51,710
For PayPal, payment history becomes a reason for shops to stay, and for AI agents to check out with PayPal.

45
0:02:52,200 --> 0:02:54,610
Real Deal Seal. Proof beats brand.

